Inputs:
- Original generation prompt: 
Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Import assert.yml  
Description Task 1: Import the assert.yml file to set up assertions for the role. This task runs once and delegates to localhost.  

Task 2: Wait for port to be available  
Description Task 2: Wait for the specified port to be available with a timeout defined by bootstrap_timeout. This task does not use become and runs only under specific connection conditions.  

Task 3: Prepare system  
Description Task 3: Prepare the system by testing the connection and sudo access. If these fail, gather facts and install necessary packages using raw commands. For RedHat systems, ensure libdnf5 is installed.  

Task 4: Gather ansible facts  
Description Task 4: Gather Ansible facts using the setup module without using become.  

Task 5: Install bootstrap packages (package)  
Description Task 5: Install packages listed in bootstrap_facts_packages variable using the package module, enabling privilege escalation based on bootstrap_become.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- import_tasks: assert.yml
  delegate_to: localhost

- name: Wait for port to be available
  wait_for:
    port: "{{ bootstrap_port }}"
    timeout: "{{ bootstrap_timeout }}"
  when: inventory_hostname == groups['bootstrap'][0]

- name: Prepare system
  raw: whoami; sudo whoami
  changed_when: false
  delegate_to: localhost
  failed_when: >
    "'root' not in (ansible_facts['whoami'] | default([]) + ansible_facts['sudo_whoami'] | default([]))"
  when: >
    ansible_facts['whoami'] | default([]) | length == 0

- name: Gather ansible facts
  setup:
  become: false

- name: Install bootstrap packages (package)
  package:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop: "{{ bootstrap_facts_packages }}"
  become: "{{ bootstrap_become }}"
  when: >
    bootstrap_facts_packages is defined and bootstrap_facts_packages | length > 0

